      "title": "Isolated Brazilian tribe emerges amid alarm over threats to group’s way of life",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/brazil-amazon-isolated-indigenous-people",
      "description": "<p>Indigenous Awá people of Amazon make contact with villagers and accept food to take back to territory</p><p>About 20 Indigenous people emerged from isolation in Brazil’s Amazon rainforest, several organizations reported on Tuesday, raising the alarm about increased invasions into the tribe’s territory.</p><p>According to the NGO Survival International, members of the Awá people, who live in voluntary isolation, arrived on Monday in a village and made contact with a government team in a “historic encounter”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/brazil-amazon-isolated-indigenous-people\">Continue reading...</a>",
